# An application names every parameter of the type. One that leaves out the
# FIRST parameter and labels another (`MapRV v: u64`, with no key type) was
# accepted: any leading argument was taken to bind the first parameter, where
# only an unlabelled one does. The map then had no key type, and the C named a
# `create` that was never written.

main: function is {
    m: MapRV v: u64
    print "\{m.length}"
}
